Let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl} ax+3, &\text{ if }x>2, \\
x-5 &\text{ if } -2 \le x \le 2, \\
2x-b &\text{ if } x <-2.
\end{array}
\right.\]Find $a+b$ if the piecewise function is continuous (which means that its graph can be drawn without lifting your pencil from the paper).

steps.text:
We can rewrite the numerator and denominator as follows:
\begin{align*}
\frac{\sin^4 x + \cos^4 x - 1}{\sin^6 x + \cos^6 x - 1} &= \frac{(\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x)^2 - 2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^6 x + \cos^6 x - 1} \\
&= \frac{1 - 2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^6 x + \cos^6 x - 1} \\
&= \frac{-2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x}{\sin^6 x + \cos^6 x - 1}.
\end{align*}

We can factor the numerator and denominator as follows:
\begin{align*}
\frac{-2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x}{\sin^6 x + \cos^6 x - 1} &= \frac{-2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x}{(\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x)(\sin^4 x - \sin^2 x \cos^2 x + \cos^4 x) - 1} \\
&= \frac{-2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x}{( \sin^4 x - \sin^2 x \cos^2 x + \cos^4 x) - 1}.
\end{align*}

We can rewrite the denominator again:
\begin{align*}
\frac{-2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x}{( \sin^4 x - \sin^2 x \cos^2 x + \cos^4 x) - 1} &= \frac{-2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x}{(\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x)^2 - 3 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x - 1} \\
&= \frac{-2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x}{1 - 3 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x - 1} \\
&= \frac{-2 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x}{- 3 \sin^2 x \cos^2 x}
\end{align*}Step

