We can compute this product:
\begin{align*}
\mathbf{M}^3 &= \begin{pmatrix} a^2 + bc & ab + bd \\ ac + cd & bc + d^2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} a^3 + abc + bcc + bcd & a^2 b + abd + b^2 c + b^2 d \\ a^2 c + acd + bcc + cd^2 & abc + bcd + bcd + d^3 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} a^3 + abc + bcc + bcd & a^2 b + abd + b^2 c + b^2 d \\ a^2 c + acd + bcc + cd^2 & abc + 2bcd + d^3 \end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}

