steps.text:
Note that
\begin{align*}
x^3 + y^3 + z^3 - 3xyz &= (x + y + z)(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - xy - xz - yz) \\
&= (x + y + z)((x + y + z)^2 - 3xy - 3xz - 3yz) \\
&= (x + y + z)^3 - 3(x + y + z)(xy + xz + yz).
\end{align*}

We have $x + y + z = 7$ and $xyz = 1.$  Also,
\begin{align*}
xy + xz + yz &= \frac{1}{x} \cdot \frac{1}{y} + \frac{1}{x} \cdot \frac{1}{z} + \frac{1}{y} \cdot \frac{1}{z} \\
&= \frac{1}{xyz} (xy + xz + yz) \\
&= (xy + xz + yz).
\end{align*}

